course: dictionary
lesson: 1416
title: Carelessness and its costs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Carelessness means not paying enough attention or care, so that mistakes or accidents happen. The word comes from care, and careless is the adjective. Carelessness is the noun, the name for the thing itself. «An oversight» means a mistake caused by carelessness, something someone forgot or missed.
explain: Read the context to see how the word is used. «Losing or breaking things through carelessness means someone has to pay to replace them.» The clue is the pay: carelessness costs money. Carelessness often appears in school reports, safety talks and stories, where a character's carelessness can start the trouble.
explain: Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. «Spoiling things on purpose in anger, or losing them by carelessness, costs money, time and sometimes someone else's work.» Here carelessness is the reason for the loss. If you put in not paying attention, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Carelessness means not paying enough attention or care, so mistakes or accidents happen.
fact: Carelessness is a noun. Careless is the adjective, so you can say «a careless mistake».
fact: «An oversight» means a mistake caused by carelessness.
fact: Losing or breaking things through carelessness means someone has to pay to replace them.
fact: Carelessness is often blamed in school reports, fires, lost things and accidents. The formal phrase is «due to carelessness».
exercise: What is carelessness? | *Not paying enough attention, so mistakes happen | Feeling tired after a long day | Being brave when something is dangerous | Paying very close attention to every detail
exercise: «Losing things through carelessness means someone has to pay to replace them.» What might someone have to do? | Get a prize for losing it | Nothing, because it costs nothing | Ask to borrow a bigger one | *Pay to replace the lost thing
exercise: Find the word that means a mistake caused by carelessness. | victory | castle | *oversight | treasure
test: Which word is the noun for not paying enough care? | *carelessness | carefully | careless | caring
test: A school report says a spilled paint pot was caused by what? | Sunshine | Kindness | *Carelessness | Magic
exam: The broken window was due to carelessness. What does due to carelessness mean? | *Caused by not paying enough care | Caused by a surprise party | Caused by a team game at break | Caused by a storm in the night
